From: Riven DS port
Subject: [PATCH] pack struct vaht_mohawk_file_table to its 10-byte on-disc size

A Mohawk file-table entry is 10 bytes on disc: uint32 offset, uint16 size-low,
uint8 size-mid, uint8 flags, uint16 unknown. Declared without packing, every
normal C ABI rounds that to 12 (the uint32 forces 4-byte alignment, so the
struct is padded to a multiple of 4).

That breaks vaht_archive_open in two ways:

  * vaht_archive.c:63 validates the entry count as
    (file_table_size - 4) / sizeof(struct vaht_mohawk_file_table). With a
    12-byte struct this never matches, so EVERY Riven archive is rejected --
    b_Data.MHK has 4607 entries and a 46074-byte table: (46074-4)/10 = 4607
    exactly, but /12 = 3839.

  * vaht_resource.c:61 and :77 fread() straight into the struct, so even past
    the check the offset and size of every resource would be read from the
    wrong bytes.

#pragma pack rather than __attribute__((packed)) so the fix also holds under
MSVC, which the DS port's converter is built with on Windows.

--- a/src/vaht_intern.h
+++ b/src/vaht_intern.h
@@ -66,13 +66,15 @@ struct vaht_mohawk_name_table
     uint16_t file_table_index; /* starting from 1 */
 };

+#pragma pack(push, 1)
 struct vaht_mohawk_file_table
 {
     uint32_t data_offset; /* absolute */
     uint16_t data_size_1; /* bits 15-0 */
     uint8_t data_size_2; /* bits 23-16 */
     uint8_t u0;
     uint16_t u1;
 };
+#pragma pack(pop)

 struct vaht_resource_s
 {
